  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="space-y-3 mb-10 not-prose">
    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm p-5">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer">What is the difference between the Alfa Laval MAB and MOPX centrifuge series?</summary>
      <p class="text-text-light mt-3 text-sm">The Alfa Laval MAB series are solid-retaining (manual-clean) <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/" class="text-navy underline hover:text-gold">disc-stack centrifuges</a>, meaning accumulated solids must be manually removed by stopping the centrifuge. The <a href="/alfa-laval-mopx-207-centrifuge/" class="text-navy underline hover:text-gold">MOPX series</a> are self-cleaning centrifuges that automatically eject separated solids during operation without stopping. MAB centrifuges are simpler and more economical for applications with lower solids loading.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm p-5">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer">What fluids can an Alfa Laval MAB centrifuge process?</summary>
      <p class="text-text-light mt-3 text-sm">Alfa Laval MAB centrifuges are designed for three-phase separation of mineral oils and fuels including <a href="/diesel-centrifuge/" class="text-navy underline hover:text-gold">diesel fuel</a>, biodiesel, turbine lube oil, hydraulic oil, and engine oil. They purify these fluids by removing water and solid contaminants simultaneously. The solids level has to be zero or close to zero for these manual clean centrifuges to be effective.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm p-5">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer">How often does an Alfa Laval MAB centrifuge need to be cleaned?</summary>
      <p class="text-text-light mt-3 text-sm">Cleaning frequency depends on the solids loading of the process fluid. For relatively clean fluids like turbine lube oil, cleaning intervals may be several days. For dirtier fluids with higher particulate content, the bowl may need manual cleaning every few hours. The sludge space capacity of each model (ranging from 0.40 gallons on the MAB 204 to 2.00 gallons on the MAB 209) also affects cleaning intervals.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm p-5">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer">Does Dolphin Centrifuge supply Alfa Laval MAB centrifuge parts?</summary>
      <p class="text-text-light mt-3 text-sm">Yes. Dolphin Centrifuge stocks and supplies Alfa Laval MAB centrifuge parts including bowl discs, gaskets, bearings, seals, gravity discs, and paring tubes for all MAB models (MAB 103, 104, 204, 205, 206, 207, 209). Contact Dolphin Centrifuge at <a href="tel:+12485222573" class="text-navy font-semibold hover:text-gold">(248) 522-2573</a> or visit <a href="/alfa-laval-centrifuge-parts/" class="text-navy underline hover:text-gold">alfa-laval-centrifuge-parts</a> for availability.</p>
